---
import SectionWrapper from '../ui/SectionWrapper.astro';
import '../../styles/components/our-work-volume.css';
---
<SectionWrapper background="luminous" class="our-work-section our-work-volume-section">
<section id="in-the-field" class="container container-wide our-work-volume" aria-labelledby="field-volume-title">
<header class="our-work-volume-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">THE COLLECTION · VOL. 04</p><h2 id="field-volume-title">In the Field</h2></div><p>Ideas become more useful when they are tested against real environments and real conversations. This volume records moments of engagement beyond the page, from university spaces to public showcases and media dialogue.</p></header>
<div class="work-volume" data-work-volume="in-the-field">
<div class="work-volume-cover" data-volume-cover><div class="work-volume-cover-art" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/media/university-speaking.webp" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><span class="work-volume-cover-wash"></span><span class="work-volume-cover-index">04</span><span class="work-volume-cover-rule"></span><span class="work-volume-cover-mark">E / D</span></div>
<div class="work-volume-cover-copy"><p class="work-volume-kicker">E DEVISER · FIELD NOTES</p><h3>Where ideas meet the world.</h3><p class="work-volume-cover-description">A documentary record of conversations, encounters, and moments beyond the studio.</p><div class="work-volume-cover-meta"><span>VOLUME 04</span><span>IN THE FIELD</span></div><button class="work-volume-open" type="button" data-volume-open aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="in-the-field-book-content"><span>Open volume</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button></div><span class="work-volume-spine" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
<div class="work-volume-content" id="in-the-field-book-content" data-volume-content hidden>
<div class="work-volume-toolbar"><div class="work-volume-location"><span class="work-volume-kicker">THE COLLECTION / 04</span><span data-volume-counter aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">01 / 03</span></div><button class="work-volume-close" type="button" data-volume-close><span>Close volume</span><span aria-hidden="true">×</span></button></div>
<div class="work-volume-pages">
<article class="work-volume-spread is-active" data-volume-page="0" aria-hidden="false"><div class="work-volume-page-copy"><p class="work-volume-page-label">01 / UNIVERSITY ENGAGEMENT</p><h3>Learning starts with listening.</h3><p>Universities bring together emerging talent, experienced practitioners, and questions that deserve thoughtful discussion. Speaking engagements create an opportunity to exchange perspectives and connect ideas with the people exploring them.</p><p>This record captures E Deviser's presence in a university setting and its participation in that wider conversation.</p><span class="work-volume-page-foot">IN THE FIELD · ACADEMIC EXCHANGE</span></div><figure class="work-volume-page-media"><img src="/media/university-speaking.webp" alt="E Deviser speaking engagement in a university setting" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption><span>04.01</span> University speaking engagement</figcaption></figure></article>
<article class="work-volume-spread" data-volume-page="1" aria-hidden="true" hidden><div class="work-volume-page-copy"><p class="work-volume-page-label">02 / LEAP SHOWCASE</p><h3>Taking ideas into the room.</h3><p>Showcases make work tangible. They create space to demonstrate thinking, encounter new perspectives, and understand how ideas are received beyond the team that developed them.</p><p>The LEAP showcase is included as a documented moment of public-facing engagement and exposure to the wider innovation ecosystem.</p><span class="work-volume-page-foot">IN THE FIELD · SHOWCASE &amp; EXPOSURE</span></div><figure class="work-volume-page-media"><img src="/media/leap-showcase.webp" alt="E Deviser at the LEAP showcase" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption><span>04.02</span> LEAP showcase</figcaption></figure></article>
<article class="work-volume-spread" data-volume-page="2" aria-hidden="true" hidden><div class="work-volume-page-copy"><p class="work-volume-page-label">03 / MEDIA CONVERSATION</p><h3>Bringing the conversation outward.</h3><p>Public dialogue is another part of putting ideas into the world. Conversations with media create an opportunity to explain the questions behind the work and contribute to a broader discussion.</p><p>This photograph records a meeting with Roze News. It is presented as a media engagement, without implying coverage or a formal media partnership.</p><span class="work-volume-page-foot">IN THE FIELD · PUBLIC DIALOGUE</span></div><figure class="work-volume-page-media"><img src="/media/roze-news-meeting.webp" alt="Documented meeting with Roze News" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><figcaption><span>04.03</span> Roze News meeting</figcaption></figure></article>
</div>
<div class="work-volume-navigation"><button type="button" data-volume-prev disabled aria-label="Previous spread"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span><span>Previous</span></button><div class="work-volume-progress" role="group" aria-label="Choose a spread"><button type="button" data-volume-go="0" class="is-active" aria-label="Go to spread 1" aria-current="step"></button><button type="button" data-volume-go="1" aria-label="Go to spread 2"></button><button type="button" data-volume-go="2" aria-label="Go to spread 3"></button></div><button type="button" data-volume-next><span>Next</span><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></button></div>
</div></section></SectionWrapper>
<script>
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-work-volume="in-the-field"]').forEach((volume) => {
const openButton=volume.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-volume-open]')!;
const closeButton=volume.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-volume-close]')!;
const content=volume.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-volume-content]')!;
const pages=Array.from(volume.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-volume-page]'));
const counter=volume.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-volume-counter]')!;
const previous=volume.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-volume-prev]')!;
const next=volume.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-volume-next]')!;
const progressButtons=Array.from(volume.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-volume-go]'));
let current=0;
const showPage=(index:number,direction:'next'|'previous'='next')=>{
if(index<0||index>=pages.length||index===current)return;
const previousPage=pages[current];const nextPage=pages[index];
previousPage.classList.remove('is-active');previousPage.setAttribute('aria-hidden','true');previousPage.hidden=true;
nextPage.hidden=false;nextPage.dataset.direction=direction;nextPage.classList.remove('is-active');
window.requestAnimationFrame(()=>nextPage.classList.add('is-active'));nextPage.setAttribute('aria-hidden','false');current=index;
counter.textContent=String(current+1).padStart(2,'0')+' / '+String(pages.length).padStart(2,'0');
previous.disabled=current===0;next.disabled=current===pages.length-1;
progressButtons.forEach((button,buttonIndex)=>{const active=buttonIndex===current;button.classList.toggle('is-active',active);if(active)button.setAttribute('aria-current','step');else button.removeAttribute('aria-current');});
};
openButton.addEventListener('click',()=>{content.hidden=false;openButton.setAttribute('aria-expanded','true');volume.classList.add('is-open');closeButton.focus();});
closeButton.addEventListener('click',()=>{volume.classList.remove('is-open');content.hidden=true;openButton.setAttribute('aria-expanded','false');openButton.focus();});
previous.addEventListener('click',()=>showPage(current-1,'previous'));next.addEventListener('click',()=>showPage(current+1,'next'));
progressButtons.forEach(button=>button.addEventListener('click',()=>{const target=Number(button.dataset.volumeGo);showPage(target,target<current?'previous':'next');}));
volume.addEventListener('keydown',event=>{if(event.key==='Escape'&&!content.hidden)closeButton.click();});
});
</script>